{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/448607-second-edition","id":448607,"title":"Second edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-18T18:57:53-07:00","id":448607,"title":"Second edition","content":"I tried to find the answer of my question on the official site but I didn't find it so here it is:<br /> <br /> Does the second edition of Werewolf (and all the others) will be *compatible* (dont know if that work make sens in english) with the rest of the white wolf book? I bought many of them, and I am concern that they will be no longer of use if they change every rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5393-enneite666","name":"Enneite666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T19:25:05-07:00","id":448649,"title":"","content":"Yes and no.<br /> <br /> Second edition introduces several new rules, and significantly changes some old ones. Gifts have a different structure. Werewolves have new traits that replace Virtue and Vice. Each shapeshifting form has unique applications. Harmony is now a balancing act between the flesh and the spirit where you actually want to be in the middle with five dots rather than push the meter too far in either direction. The Condition system is introduced to combine circumstantial modifiers with dramatic incentives. There's a lot of thematic focus on the hunt.<br /> <br /> It doesn't, however, completely upend the nature of the Storytelling System. You've still got the same lists of Attributes and Skills. You still roll dice in the same way with the same results. You still have Primal Urge and the five forms of Renown. You're still the Uratha, you've still got the auspices and the tribes and lodges and tribal totems and you still patrol the balance between flesh and spirit, in the form of the Hisil/Shadow. As such, a lot of stuff that refers to these traits and elements will still work fine, even in a new context of how those elements work.<br /> <br /> Some aspects of books will be more useful than others. Gifts might need tweaking to make them suitably useful and fit them into the unlock-Gifts-through-Renown model of the new system, but individual powers are still going to follow the general pattern, roll this dice pool, count successes, dramatic failure/failure/success/exceptional success, so a surprising amount of old powers are largely unaffected by the 2e changes. Weapon stats from 1E can generally be converted to 2E simply by making bashing weapons lethal and reducing their weapon rating by 1 (because the rating, instead of adding dice, directly adds to damage on a successful attack now). A lot of setting material will be pretty much straight usable with no alteration necessary. The book on The Pure, for example, was cited as a direct focus for the vision of the Pure in the 2e corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T19:27:56-07:00","id":448654,"title":"","content":"They are more or less compatible. Some things you will need to do a little work to convert, but mostly you can still use 1st edition material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T19:28:31-07:00","id":448655,"title":"","content":"A lot of the 'fluff' stuff is still valid, and the mechanics are, at least in some areas, easy to transfer over. Gifts not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T20:13:31-07:00","id":448731,"title":"","content":"key fluff that is no longer valid being the unihar, which btw eliminates the &quot;breeder&quot; idigam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T01:48:07-07:00","id":448940,"title":"","content":"Just to be clear, when you say White Wolf Books, which one do you mean? nWoD (Requiem, Forsaken, Awakening...), in most cases Yes. The Changes are broad, but you can convert it easily. But unfortunately the second edition of the nWoD worth it to put the first edition in the shelf and just use it for the Fluff.<br /> Except for Demon (and Mummy I guess), because the new rules are already included.<br /> <br /> If you mean oWoD (Masquerade, Apocalypse, Ascension...), No! 2E is not compatible with the old World of Darkness, but it doesn\u2019t have to. Since second Edition the World is such unique, that oWod and nWod 2E are truly different games with similar themes now. You can't mix them, but you can play both with out the feeling of playing a copy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T08:20:31-07:00","id":449288,"title":"","content":"I mean the new world of darkness, such as tribes of the moon, book of spirit, road of midninght, dogs of war, hunter the vigil, etc...<br /> <br /> The merits system stay the same ? Is the gifts system the biggest change ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5393,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5393-enneite666","user":"Enneite666","date":". 03-19-2015, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5393-enneite666","name":"Enneite666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T08:27:32-07:00","id":449294,"title":"","content":"Not sure how comparable merits are. And yes lodges, tribes, signs et al are still canon fluff wise, baring the obvious changes in this book. Feel free to use the tribes as you see in tribes of the moon!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T08:27:49-07:00","id":449295,"title":"","content":"Merit's <i>work </i>the same, although a fair few have been re-jigged. But porting from older books should not be a problem at all in most cases. <br /> <br /> Spirits are mostly the same, except the numina used to muck about in the mortal world are now a separate thing called &quot;manifestations&quot; which have a new system of conditions they work in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T08:39:16-07:00","id":449301,"title":"","content":"Merits use the same system, but a lot of Merits have been re-written. The way experience is awarded is different, so the way character elements are priced has changed accordingly. Combat works largely the same way, with a few not insignificant changes. The gift system has changed quite a lot, but for the better. Harmony is very different. Primal urge works basically the same, but the benefits come much faster and the drawbacks have changed so you have to be proactive to mitigate them rather than encouraging sedentary. The forms have slightly different benefits. Death Rage works very differently. But for the most part, elements from 1e books can still be used in 2e, with minimal tinkering to convert to the new systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T09:32:38-07:00","id":449372,"title":"","content":"Mechanically, Gifts from earlier books are not particularly compatible. Rites can often be translated without too much difficulty, but they do work differently to 1e rites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}